[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. It held three problems. The reports
were merged because they sound alike, not because they share a cause. Each problem now has its
own ticket, and all three are closed. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: the parser is
fixed, and the booking-v3 hint won't be fixed because that form is retired.

<Callout>
Resolved. `parser`: fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). `hint`: won't fix, booking-v3
form retired. `oneDayMove`: closed as a duplicate of `parser`, where the desk files it.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="tmaconnelly/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows" />

Counts are the desk's own view: each report id once, placed by its tenant (`#lib/kb/causes`).
The one-day moves stay counted where they're filed, under `parser`, so their ticket is a part of
`parser`'s count, not extra.

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Our tenants write the day
first, so 7 April comes out as 4 July. Every tenant on file is day first, so every tenant is hit,
through the app, email and the booking-v2 form. Day and month swap exactly; the weekday follows
the wrong date.

**`hint`: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** At a day-first tenant on
booking-v3, people type what the hint tells them, month first, and the form reads it the tenant's
way. The result looks like the parser bug, but only through that form, and fixing the parser
does not touch it. Won't fix: the booking-v3 form is retired, so the hint goes with it.

**`oneDayMove`: some dates move by one day.** These are not swaps. Tuesday 12 May shows as
Monday 11 May; a meeting reads Tuesday in Lisbon and Monday in Toronto; an invite arrives before
the booking was made. That points to a time-zone or midnight-UTC bug. The desk read them as a
one-day move and files them under `parser` by tenant; their ticket is closed as a duplicate of
`parser`'s, so they are tracked there.

## How each report was placed

1. Count each report id once.
2. By tenant: a day-first tenant's report through booking-v3's form is `hint`; any other report
   from a day-first tenant is `parser`. No tenant on file: `unplaced`.
3. Reports in the desk notes as a one-day move are also listed as `oneDayMove`, inside the count
   they're filed under.

Intake's tag is not used. It is a guess from the reporter's browser.

## The desk's table

The table on #4471, as exported. It already showed `hint` as "not this ticket", with no ticket of
its own:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Why they were merged

Merging by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) puts
"Date is wrong" from a parser bug and "Date is wrong" from a form hint in one ticket. Subject is
what the reporter felt, not what broke.

## What to change

- Merge on cause (tenant, channel, form), not on subject. [Triage](/kb/triage/dedupe) needs a
  new decision record to replace 0001.
- Watch for one-day moves after the parser fix: if they keep coming, `oneDayMove` gets reopened
  as its own fix.

